<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 22.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 22.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on January 21. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		   P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1   Tourism Asset	 3566.67    1.07</p>
<p>2   Portman Min	    363.49    2.29</p>
<p>3   Niugini Min	    213.67    2.97</p>
<p>4   Countrywide-PP	 185.48    1.15</p>
<p>5   Mayne Nickless	 175.50    7.95</p>
<p>6   Colonial Coml	  122.95    2.25</p>
<p>7   Adel Bton Cement     119.57    1.65</p>
<p>8   Energy Equity	   84.89    1.18</p>
<p>9   Forrestania Gold	84.23    2.35</p>
<p>10  Herald Rsc		84.07    0.95</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
